---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
const schema=[
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Oculivo","applicationCategory":"BusinessApplication","operatingSystem":"Web","url":"https://oculivo.com/optical-management/","description":"Optical management software for frame inventory, contact lenses, patient orders, vendors, receiving, dispensing and connected eye-care practice workflows."},
  {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
    {"@type":"Question","name":"What should optical management software track?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Useful optical workflows include frames, contact lenses, vendors, inventory movement, patient orders, receiving, status, dispensing and connected billing context."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Why connect optical inventory to the patient record?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Connecting optical activity to the patient record keeps product selection, order status, communication, billing and dispensing history together."}}
  ]}
]
---
<Base title="Optical Inventory & Order Management Software | Oculivo" description="Optical management software for frame inventory, contact lenses, patient orders, vendors, receiving, dispensing and connected eye-care practice workflows." schema={schema}>
<main>
<section class="hero-dark page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero-icon">◉</div><span class="eyebrow">Optical inventory management</span><h1>Optical inventory and orders<br/>connected to the patient.</h1><p>Manage frames, contact lenses, vendors, inventory movement, patient orders, receiving, status, dispensing, communication and billing without separating optical from the rest of the practice.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn-grad" href="https://taxrescrm.app/book?product=oculivo">Request a private demo&nbsp; →</a><a class="btn-outline" href="/pricing/">View pricing</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section-light depth-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="depth-top"><span class="eyebrow">Connected optical operations</span><div class="depth-title"><h2>Know what is in stock, on order and ready for the patient.</h2><p>Optical workflows stay tied to the same patient, communication, billing and reporting context used by the rest of the practice.</p></div></div><div class="depth-cards"><article class="depth-card"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Frame + contact lens inventory</h3><p>Track products, vendors, on-hand quantity, receiving and movement history with clear practice ownership.</p><small>Read the <a href="/resources/optical-inventory-management-guide/">optical inventory management guide</a></small></article><article class="depth-card"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Patient orders</h3><p>Keep frame, lens, contact lens and fulfillment details connected from selection through vendor or lab processing.</p><small>See the <a href="/resources/optical-order-tracking-workflow/">optical order tracking workflow</a></small></article><article class="depth-card"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Receiving + dispensing</h3><p>Make receiving, quality checks, ready status and dispensing part of the patient history rather than a separate stockroom process.</p><small>Patient communication and billing stay connected</small></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section-light"><div class="wrap article-wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Optical operations</span><h2>Inventory counts are only useful when the movement history is clear.</h2><p>A strong optical workflow should explain why inventory changed, which patient an order belongs to and what happens next. That means receiving, patient allocation, order status, dispensing and adjustment history should remain visible in one operational record.</p><section class="article-section"><h3>Track products with consistent data</h3><p>Brand, model, color, size, cost, retail context and vendor information make inventory counts and purchasing decisions more reliable.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h3>Separate stock from patient-allocated orders</h3><p>Staff should be able to distinguish available inventory from product that is reserved, on order or already tied to a patient.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h3>Connect optical activity to revenue</h3><p>Patient balances, product status and dispensing history are easier to understand when optical and billing workflows use the same patient context.</p></section></div></section>
<section class="founding-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="founding-card"><div><span class="eyebrow">See the workflow</span><h2>Walk through your optical operation in Oculivo.</h2><p>Review inventory, patient orders, receiving, communication, billing and dispensing in a private demo.</p></div><a class="btn-white" href="https://taxrescrm.app/book?product=oculivo">Request your private demo&nbsp; →</a></div></div></section>
</main>
</Base>
<style>.article-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding-top:4.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem}.article-wrap>h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.2rem);margin:.8rem 0 1rem;color:#0f172a}.article-wrap>p,.article-section p{font-size:1.04rem;line-height:1.8;color:#475569}.article-section{padding:1.25rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(15,23,42,.08)}.article-section h3{font-size:1.25rem;margin:0 0 .55rem;color:#0f172a}.depth-card a{color:inherit}</style>